  "notes": "37 mm gearmotor with a two-channel Hall encoder on the rear shaft (about 11 pulses per motor turn per channel, times the gear ratio). Output shaft 6 mm D, 17 mm, pointing down (-z), face at z=0 like dc-gearmotor-12v-37. 6-pin cable: M1 / M2 motor, then encoder GND, 3.3-5 V, A, B. Needs a driver: never a GPIO pin. Encoder outputs swing to the encoder supply (3.3 V from the board).",
